---
// Fig. for "Quadratic Residues & Square Roots": where these tools show
// up — mirrors the three-column summary pattern used by the entropy and
// Euclid/CRT/Euler lessons' closing figures.
---
<svg viewBox="0 0 760 430" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" style="width:100%;height:auto;display:block;">
  <text x="380" y="26" text-anchor="middle" fill="#e9eef5" font-size="16" font-weight="800" font-family="-apple-system,Arial,sans-serif">where these tools show up</text>

  <!-- the square test -->
  <rect x="30" y="56" width="220" height="230" rx="12" fill="#121c2c" stroke="#3ab7ff" stroke-width="1.8" />
  <text x="140" y="90" text-anchor="middle" fill="#8fdcff" font-size="14.5" font-weight="800" font-family="-apple-system,Arial,sans-serif">THE SQUARE TEST</text>
  <text x="140" y="130" text-anchor="middle" fill="#c3cedd" font-size="12" font-family="-apple-system,Arial,sans-serif">is this number a square?</text>
  <text x="140" y="148" text-anchor="middle" fill="#c3cedd" font-size="12" font-family="-apple-system,Arial,sans-serif">one exponentiation</text>
  <text x="140" y="166" text-anchor="middle" fill="#c3cedd" font-size="12" font-family="-apple-system,Arial,sans-serif">answers it</text>
  <text x="140" y="256" text-anchor="middle" fill="#5ddc8a" font-size="12.5" font-style="italic" font-family="-apple-system,Arial,sans-serif">A fast yes or no.</text>

  <!-- square roots -->
  <rect x="270" y="56" width="220" height="230" rx="12" fill="#121c2c" stroke="#5ddc8a" stroke-width="1.8" />
  <text x="380" y="90" text-anchor="middle" fill="#5ddc8a" font-size="14.5" font-weight="800" font-family="-apple-system,Arial,sans-serif">SQUARE ROOTS</text>
  <text x="380" y="130" text-anchor="middle" fill="#c3cedd" font-size="12" font-family="-apple-system,Arial,sans-serif">a shortcut when p leaves</text>
  <text x="380" y="148" text-anchor="middle" fill="#c3cedd" font-size="12" font-family="-apple-system,Arial,sans-serif">remainder 3 mod 4,</text>
  <text x="380" y="166" text-anchor="middle" fill="#c3cedd" font-size="12" font-family="-apple-system,Arial,sans-serif">and Tonelli&#8211;Shanks</text>
  <text x="380" y="184" text-anchor="middle" fill="#c3cedd" font-size="12" font-family="-apple-system,Arial,sans-serif">otherwise</text>
  <text x="380" y="256" text-anchor="middle" fill="#5ddc8a" font-size="12.5" font-style="italic" font-family="-apple-system,Arial,sans-serif">Solving y&#178; = a.</text>

  <!-- compression and hash-to-curve -->
  <rect x="510" y="56" width="220" height="230" rx="12" fill="#121c2c" stroke="#8fdcff" stroke-width="1.8" />
  <text x="620" y="84" text-anchor="middle" fill="#8fdcff" font-size="14.5" font-weight="800" font-family="-apple-system,Arial,sans-serif">COMPRESSION AND</text>
  <text x="620" y="104" text-anchor="middle" fill="#8fdcff" font-size="14.5" font-weight="800" font-family="-apple-system,Arial,sans-serif">HASH-TO-CURVE</text>
  <text x="620" y="140" text-anchor="middle" fill="#c3cedd" font-size="12" font-family="-apple-system,Arial,sans-serif">store one bit instead of y,</text>
  <text x="620" y="158" text-anchor="middle" fill="#c3cedd" font-size="12" font-family="-apple-system,Arial,sans-serif">and map data onto</text>
  <text x="620" y="176" text-anchor="middle" fill="#c3cedd" font-size="12" font-family="-apple-system,Arial,sans-serif">the curve</text>
  <text x="620" y="256" text-anchor="middle" fill="#5ddc8a" font-size="12.5" font-style="italic" font-family="-apple-system,Arial,sans-serif">Points from numbers.</text>

  <line x1="30" y1="316" x2="730" y2="316" stroke="#223049" stroke-width="1" />
  <text x="380" y="340" text-anchor="middle" fill="#8fdcff" font-size="15.5" font-weight="800" font-family="-apple-system,Arial,sans-serif">ONE TEST, ONE ROOT, ONE BIT</text>
  <text x="380" y="362" text-anchor="middle" fill="#8b96a8" font-size="12.5" font-family="-apple-system,Arial,sans-serif">Next up: extension fields and towers.</text>
</svg>
